class:: LatoocarfianMap
summary:: Trigger-driven raw Latoocarfian map coordinates
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/LatoocarfianSonify, Classes/CliffordMap

description::

Uses the documented recurrence code::x' = sin(b*y) + c*sin(b*x):: and code::y' = sin(a*x) + d*sin(a*y)::. Latoocarfian variants circulate; this project uses this equation consistently in server code, tests, and the sonifier.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, it advances once per trigger edge; unlike Stepper, it maintains two coupled trigonometric state coordinates.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::latoocarfian-map-phase.png#A Latoocarfian attractor at the documented defaults. x is horizontal and y is vertical; point density reveals how often the orbit visits each region.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on a rising edge.
argument:: a
Frequency coefficient used in the y equation.
argument:: b
Frequency coefficient used in the x equation.
argument:: c
Second sine weight in the x equation.
argument:: d
Second sine weight in the y equation.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate.
argument:: reset
Restore supplied initial coordinates on a rising edge.
Returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ LatoocarfianMap.ar(Impulse.ar(600))[1] * 0.1 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ VarSaw.ar(LatoocarfianMap.kr(Impulse.kr(20))[0].linexp(-1.5, 1.5, 60, 3000), 0, 0.2, 0.08) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Latoocarfian map: x-y phase portrait",
    [-1.6, 1.6], [-1.6, 1.6],
    { LatoocarfianMap.kr(Impulse.kr(120)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(-1.6, 1.6).linexp(-1.6, 1.6, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(-1.6, 1.6).linlin(-1.6, 1.6, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::

